---
// -- SEO COPY REWRITE APPLIED, 16 September 2026 -------------------------
//
// This page has been rewritten against tile-and-grout-cleaning-copy-rewrite.md
// (workbook row 10, primary `tile and grout cleaning` 700/mo, cluster
// 1,480/mo). Section numbers in the comments below are that brief's, and it
// SUPERSEDES the "NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS" note below.
//
// THIS IS THE LIGHTEST REWRITE IN EITHER BATCH, AND THAT IS THE FINDING. The
// brief scores this page 84, the strongest of the four reviewed, and says so
// outright: the page already carried the mapped phrase in the title, the URL,
// the opening paragraph, a heading and the meta, and it already covers its
// whole mapped cluster, 1,480 of 1,480. Fourteen of its sections are marked
// No change because they are already doing their job. What was holding it
// back is not the words.
//
// So only four things changed in copy: the approved title and meta, the H1
// (with the old one demoted to open the hero lead), the approved CTA in four
// places, and the two FAQ headings. Plus the narrowed comparison table and
// the full-footprint town list.
//
// DELIBERATELY NO NEW SECTION, unlike the other three pages in these two
// batches. All seven mapped terms are word-order variants of one intent and
// the page serves it thoroughly, so there is no gap in the cluster to write
// against. The live SERP does show the significant Australian competitors
// built around grout sealing, colour sealing, regrouting, shower repairs and
// anti-slip treatment, and NONE of those terms is in the mapped cluster, but
// there is no demand connector available to size that. It is raised as a
// question for the workbook owner rather than written up here. Adding copy
// against unsourced demand is how pages get padded.
//
// 🔴 TWO BLOCKING CHANGE REQUESTS ARE OPEN AND SHIP UNRESOLVED,
// both against the approved meta description and both set out in full at
// `pageMeta` below: it promises the original colour back, which this page's
// own strongest section argues against, and it states "Sealing available"
// while the page asks twice whether TLB offers it. The approved text is
// placed per Rule 3. DO NOT PUBLISH THE META until the workbook owner rules.
//
// Not done here, because they are not copy: the URL mismatch (folder level
// only, no keyword cost either way, so it is a redirect decision for the
// build team), the canonical domain, FAQ schema for ten questions across two
// blocks, dropping the header's competing "Get an instant quote", and hiding
// the testimonial block until real quotes exist.
//
// Tile and grout cleaning — one of the six "Appliances" leaf pages under the
// Home Cleaning mega-menu. See carpet-and-rug-cleaning.astro for the shared
// reasoning behind this group, and src/data/appliance-services.ts for the
// cluster links.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS. All copy is DRAFTED from the brand foundation
// document. Facts only TLB holds ship as visible [brackets].
//
// ⚠️ THIS PAGE OVERLAPS /house-cleaning/mould-removal/ AND MUST DEFER TO IT.
// Black spotting in shower grout is the single most common reason someone
// searches this topic, and it is very often mould. That page is the most
// constrained on the site: it makes NO health claim, promises no permanent
// removal, and is explicit that TLB cleans surface mould only and is not a
// remediation business. This page must not quietly undercut any of that by
// treating mould as an ordinary cleaning problem.
//
// So: this page names mould once, says plainly that discoloured grout is
// often mould rather than dirt, and sends the reader there. It makes no
// health claim, offers no method for it, and promises nothing about it
// staying gone. Do not expand that. If a reader wants the mould answer, the
// answer is the mould page.
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH:
//   - SEALING. §4's last card and branded FAQ 4 both offer to reseal grout
//     after cleaning. That is a genuinely separate service with its own
//     product, cost and cure time. Confirm TLB does it. If not, both need to
//     change from an offer to a recommendation the customer arranges.
//   - EQUIPMENT. The page describes a rotary/pressure tool with capture, not
//     a hand brush. Confirm what TLB actually uses; if it is hand scrubbing,
//     say so plainly, because hand scrubbing is honest and slow rather than
//     inferior, and the copy should not imply machinery that does not exist.
//   - Pricing basis bracketed.
//
// PHOTOGRAPHY: hero is a family B cut-out keyed against green (a pale grey
// tiled floor cannot be keyed off white). See
// src/assets/home_cleaning/appliances/IMAGE-PROMPTS.md.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/sections/SiteHeader.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import Backdrop from '../../components/ui/Backdrop.astro';
import TextBlock from '../../components/sections/TextBlock.astro';
import PathwayCards from '../../components/sections/PathwayCards.astro';
import ServiceBlocks from '../../components/sections/ServiceBlocks.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import TagCloud from '../../components/sections/TagCloud.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/sections/ComparisonTable.astro';
import GoogleReviewSlider from '../../components/sections/GoogleReviewSlider.astro';
import { googleBusinessProfileUrl, googleReviews } from '../../data/googleReviews';
import Faq from '../../components/sections/Faq.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/sections/CallToAction.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/sections/SiteFooter.astro';
import logoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-horizontal.png';
// Pathway cards: real TLB photos (6 Oct 2026), 4:3 crops of the team's
// shower-clean video frames. Card 1 is the hero's frame cropped tighter, so
// the two read as different shots.
import cardTeamImg from '../../assets/home_cleaning/appliances/tile_and_grout/tile-and-grout-cleaner-tidying-a-shower-niche.jpg';
import { whoIsInYourHomeCard } from '../../data/whoIsInYourHome';
import footerLogoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-square.png';
import {
  primaryNav,
  headerNav,
  headerSecondaryCta,
  footerServiceLinks,
  footerContact,
  footerCopyright,
  quoteCta,
} from '../../data/navigation';
import { comparisonColumns, serviceComparisonRows } from '../../data/comparison';
import { footprintLocationGroups, footprintSubheading } from '../../data/locations';
import { trustBarCards } from '../../data/trust';
import { otherApplianceServices } from '../../data/appliance-services';
import { theLineHeading, howItWorks, managedForYou, theLineBody } from '../../data/brand-lines';
import { localBusiness } from '../../data/business';
import { z } from 'astro/zod';
import { getPage } from '../../lib/cms';
import * as section from '../../lib/cms-schemas';
import { sized } from '../../lib/cms-schemas';

const OWN_HREF = '/house-cleaning/tile-and-grout-cleaning/';

// In `pageMeta`, on `title`:
// Approved title, pasted verbatim from the brief (workbook row 10) per its
// Rule 3. "Services" picks up `tile and grout cleaning services` 250/mo and
// `professional tile and grout cleaning services` 200/mo (Keyword Mapping &
// Metadata, 15 Sep 2026). The ampersand is a deliberate shortener and the
// phrase still reads as the mapped term.
// In `pageMeta`, on `description`:
// 🔴 TWO BLOCKING CHANGE REQUESTS AGAINST THIS APPROVED META. It is
// pasted verbatim per Rule 3, and IT SHOULD NOT GO LIVE until the workbook
// owner resolves both. See the file header for the full argument.
//
//   ONE. It promises "brings back the original colour". The page's bleach
//   section says, in the strongest writing on the site: "Grout will not
//   always come back to white, and any cleaner who promises it will is
//   either about to disappoint you or about to do something you did not
//   agree to." That is not a tension. It is the page calling its own meta
//   description a warning sign. Suggested replacement for the workbook,
//   147 characters, keeping the CTA and the rooms:
//     "Tile and grout cleaning that brings the colour back as far as it
//      will come, in bathrooms, kitchens and entryways. Sealing available.
//      Get a fixed quote today."
//
//   TWO. It states "Sealing available" as fact. This page carries TWO live
//   placeholders asking whether TLB offers sealing at all (method stage
//   six, and branded FAQ 4), and the cost FAQ assumes it as a third. The
//   meta asserts it, the page asks about it. One of the two has to change
//   and the answer is not a copy decision.
//
// Worth telling the workbook owner: the LIVE meta being replaced already
// got this right, with "brought back as far as it will come, with an honest
// answer on the rest". The correct wording exists and does not need
// inventing. 140 characters; the live one was 164 and over the limit.

// The primary CTA, defined once and repeated in four places per BFD 9.5: the
// hero button, pathway card 1, the button after the six stages and the
// closing block.
//
// NO BLOCKING CONFLICT ON THE CTA ITSELF, unlike the meta above. This fixes a
// live breach: the page says in its own words that "the honest answer is a
// fast quote rather than an instant one", and then put "Get an instant quote"
// on four buttons, which BFD 13.2 rules out on condition-driven work.
// "Fixed" is also the accurate word here, because the page promises you will
// know the price before work starts, not after.

// In `hero`, on `headingLines`:
// Brief section 4. This was the only component on the page's primary
// keyword score that still missed, worth 15 points scored present or
// absent, on a mapped phrase of 700/mo. Naming the three areas is the
// specificity BFD 14 asks for rather than decoration.
// In `hero`, on `lead`:
// ON DEMOTING A GOOD LINE: "The tiles are fine. It is the lines between
// them." is the sharpest headline on the site. It is NOT being cut. It
// lands one line lower, opening the lead, and still does the same work,
// because the argument it makes is the argument the whole page runs on.
// Hero has no separate subheading slot; `headingLines` all render inside
// the one <h1>.
//
// The hero paragraph after it is UNCHANGED, per brief section 6: it
// already carries the mapped phrase contiguously inside its first
// sentence, which is the full 10-point opening-paragraph component, and
// its second sentence is the honest version of what the approved meta
// overpromises. Nothing to improve.
// In `hero`, on `image`:
// A real TLB photo since 6 Oct 2026, replacing the transparent cut-out
// (which ran with `contain-bottom`). Default `cover` fit now. The file is
// a near-square crop (1080x1150) from the bottom of a tall video frame:
// this page's long heading and lead make the desktop panel roughly square,
// and a 4:3 crop there trimmed the sides and read as zoomed in. Near
// square, the panel shows the photo's full width with the shower hose
// above her. `ratio` is the mobile fallback.

// In `methodItems`, on "Rinsed and lifted, not wiped":
// ⚠️ LAUNCH BLOCKER. Confirm the equipment. See the file header.
// In `methodItems`, on "Sealing, if it is worth it":
// ⚠️ LAUNCH BLOCKER. Confirm TLB seals. See the file header.

// Deferral to the mould page. A Callout, not a TextBlock: it is a short
// aside, and SECTIONS.md is clear that is what Callout is for.
//
// ⚠️ DO NOT EXPAND THIS. See the file header. No health claim, no method, no
// promise it stays gone. The mould page owns all of that.

const clusterServices = otherApplianceServices(OWN_HREF);

// In `comparisonTable`, on `rows`:
// Brief section 20, scorecard finding 7. The holiday-lets row comes off:
// the other seven bear on a household booking a grout clean, and this one
// is about a service the page does not sell. "Who cleans your home" is
// correct here and stays. See data/comparison.ts.

// In `brandedFaqItems`, on "Should we seal the grout afterwards?":
// ⚠️ Depends on the sealing launch blocker in the file header.

// §12 Non-branded FAQs.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFICATION PASS. Checkable claims here:
//   - Grout is cement based and porous. Correct.
//   - Acidic cleaners etch natural stone. Correct and important.
//   - Bleach degrades grout with repeated use and does not remove embedded
//     soil. Correct in substance and widely documented in trade guidance.
//   - ⚠️ NEVER MIX BLEACH WITH ACID OR AMMONIA. This is a genuine safety
//     point, it is the one piece of safety advice on this page, and it is
//     stated as a prohibition with no method attached, exactly as
//     house-cleaning/mould-removal.astro handles the same warning. BFD 5.3
//     bars advice that could cause harm if followed incorrectly, so this
//     tells the reader what NOT to do and nothing else. Do not expand it
//     into a how-to or name a safe alternative product.
//
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on "How much does tile and grout cleaning cost?":
// ⚠️ BRACKETED ON PURPOSE, same as every sibling.

// CONTENT lives in src/content/pages/house-cleaning/tile-and-grout-cleaning.yaml
// and is edited in Pages CMS ("Tile and grout cleaning"). This file owns the
// layout. The notes above explain why each section says what it says; they
// stay here because Pages CMS rewrites the YAML on save and would drop them.
const page = await getPage(
  'house-cleaning/tile-and-grout-cleaning',
  z.object({
    seo: section.seo,
    // The text of the page's one primary button. It always links to the
    // site-wide quote page, so only the words are editable.
    buttonLabel: section.text,
    hero: section.hero,
    // Its background photo sits behind the trust bar and this block together
    // (the Backdrop below), so it cannot be left empty.
    definition: section.textBlock.extend({ backgroundImage: section.backgroundPhoto }),
    // The third card is the shared "Who is in my home" card, added in code.
    // A card whose button is left empty gets the page's primary button.
    pathways: section.pathwayCards.extend({
      cards: z.array(section.pathwayCards.shape.cards.element.extend({ cta: section.optional(section.link) })).min(1),
    }),
    method: section.iconGrid,
    mould: section.callout,
    bleach: section.textBlock,
    // The rows are the shared appliance cross-links.
    otherServices: section.sectionIntro,
    // The columns and rows are the shared comparison table (Site settings).
    comparison: section.comparisonTable.omit({ columns: true, rows: true }),
    reviews: section.sectionHeading,
    // The subheading, like the towns, is the shared one for every full band.
    whereWeClean: section.tagCloud.omit({ subheading: true }),
    bookingFaq: section.faq,
    generalFaq: section.faq,
    closingCta: section.callToAction,
  }),
);

const pageMeta = {
  ...page.seo,
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/house-cleaning/tile-and-grout-cleaning/',
};

const business = localBusiness({
  description: pageMeta.description,
  areaServed: 'Northern Rivers NSW and Southern Gold Coast QLD',
  sameAs: googleBusinessProfileUrl ? [googleBusinessProfileUrl] : [],
});

const pageCta = { label: page.buttonLabel, href: quoteCta.href };

const heroImage = page.hero.image && sized(page.hero.image, '1/1');

const pathwayCards = [
  ...page.pathways.cards.map((card, i) => ({
    number: i + 1,
    ...card,
    image: sized(card.image, '4/3'),
    cta: card.cta ?? pageCta,
  })),
  whoIsInYourHomeCard(cardTeamImg, 'A TLB cleaner straightening the bottles in a tiled shower niche'),
];

---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="right"
      kicker={page.hero.kicker}
      headingLines={page.hero.headingLines}
      subheading={page.hero.subheading}
      lead={page.hero.lead}
      cta={page.hero.cta ?? pageCta}
      image={heroImage}
    />

    <Backdrop image={page.definition.backgroundImage} tint="muted" opacity={90}>
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock
        theme="muted"
        align="left"
        heading={page.definition.heading}
        body={page.definition.body}
        cta={page.definition.cta}
      />
    </Backdrop>

    <PathwayCards heading={page.pathways.heading} headingAccent={page.pathways.headingAccent} cards={pathwayCards} />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="icon-grid"
      heading={page.method.heading}
      lead={page.method.lead}
      items={page.method.items}
      note={page.method.note}
      cta={pageCta}
    />

    <Callout tone="note" heading={page.mould.heading} body={page.mould.body} cta={page.mould.cta} />

    <TextBlock
      theme="dark"
      align="left"
      heading={page.bleach.heading}
      body={page.bleach.body}
      cta={page.bleach.cta}
      backgroundImage={page.bleach.backgroundImage}
    />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading={page.otherServices.heading}
      lead={page.otherServices.lead}
      items={clusterServices.map((service) => ({
        icon: 'spray-bottle' as const,
        title: service.label,
        description: service.blurb,
        href: service.href,
      }))}
    />

    <ComparisonTable
      heading={page.comparison.heading}
      cornerLabel={page.comparison.cornerLabel}
      lead={page.comparison.lead}
      columns={comparisonColumns}
      rows={serviceComparisonRows()}
      footnote={page.comparison.footnote}
      cta={page.comparison.cta}
    />

    <GoogleReviewSlider heading={page.reviews.heading} reviews={googleReviews} profileUrl={googleBusinessProfileUrl} />

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.whereWeClean.heading}
      subheading={footprintSubheading}
      tags={page.whereWeClean.tags}
      groups={footprintLocationGroups}
      note={page.whereWeClean.note}
    />

    {/* §1.3 The Line as a section heading, with §1.4 as its standfirst.
        The copy, and the reason this page gets `fast` rather than the other
        variant, both live in data/brand-lines.ts. Change it there, not here.

        `muted`, not `dark`: TagCloud above paints --color-brand and Faq below
        paints --color-surface, so Cream between them keeps the page
        alternating instead of stacking two dark bands.

        No CTA prop. §9.5 wants one primary CTA per page, repeated, and the
        closing CallToAction is directly under the FAQs. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading={theLineHeading.fast}
      body={[managedForYou.oneOff, ...theLineBody.residential, ...howItWorks.general]}
    />

    {/* Brief sections 24 and 25. The page carried two FAQ headings and the
        pair read as a build error. This block is about working with TLB, the
        next is about the service. Sentence case is BFD 9.2, and the mapped
        phrase stays contiguous either way, so no keyword is at risk.

        PROTECT non-branded question 2. It carries the only safety
        information on the site, that bleach must never be mixed with an
        acidic cleaner, with ammonia or with any other product. It is
        correct, and it is the kind of passage an AI assistant surfaces.
        Never cut it, and do not soften the warning symbol.

        PROTECT non-branded question 3. The cleaning / sealing / regrouting
        distinction is the clearest explanation of the category anywhere in
        the competitive set, and it ends by saying cleaning cannot fix grout
        that is physically gone. That sentence costs bookings and earns
        trust, which is the trade BFD 2.3 asks for. */}
    <Faq heading={page.bookingFaq.heading} lead={page.bookingFaq.lead} items={page.bookingFaq.items} />
    <Faq heading={page.generalFaq.heading} lead={page.generalFaq.lead} items={page.generalFaq.items} />

    <CallToAction
      variant="secondary"
      kicker={page.closingCta.kicker}
      heading={page.closingCta.heading}
      lead={page.closingCta.lead}
      cta={page.closingCta.cta ?? pageCta}
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: footerLogoImg }}
    columns={[
      { title: 'Services', links: footerServiceLinks },
      { title: 'Locations', links: [{ label: 'View all locations', href: '/locations/' }] },
    ]}
    contact={footerContact}
    copyright={footerCopyright}
  />
</Base>
